From a7868a069dcbf158d08d9c91699efba87527da74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:49:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rednsd: DNS-over-TLS for the LAN, and the encrypted-DNS block
 lists

rednsd answers DNS-over-TLS on port 853 of the LAN bridges with the router's
certificate and forwards to the local resolver, adding the client's address so
Dreadwatch, Wallguard and DNS Director judge the real device. Connections,
pending queries, file descriptors and write buffers are capped per device; it
runs as nobody and exits on a certificate or bind error rather than loop.
encdns.sh keeps the DoH resolver address sets for "Block encrypted DNS that
goes around the router": the shipped seed plus a maintained list, validated as
the kernel reads it - private, loopback, link-local and multicast ranges
refused, nothing wider than IPv4 /24 or IPv6 /48, IPv6 capped at its set's
size - cached on /jffs and replayed at boot. doh-names.txt: the DoH provider
names answered NXDOMAIN while the block is on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
